[{"id": "9748243", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "bda4edf", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "shortcode", "settings": {"shortcode": "[rank_math_breadcrumb]"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "00d218a", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "How to bathe your dog", "header_size": "h1"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "7eb9561", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>You want to wash your dog without irritating their skin or eyes, and get them properly dry afterward. Here's how to prepare, bathe, rinse and dry, step by step.</p>", "typography_typography": "custom", "__globals__": {"typography_typography": "globals/typography?id=secondary"}}, "elements": []}, {"id": "0e4fbc6", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>By Grooming Dogs · Updated {{UPDATED}}</p>", "text_color": "#5B6870", "__globals__": {"typography_typography": "globals/typography?id=accent", "text_color": "globals/colors?id=secondary"}}, "elements": []}, {"id": "11f6d0c", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>How often to bathe depends on your dog's coat. See <a href=\"/how-often-should-you-groom-your-dog/\">how often to bathe your dog</a>. If your dog fights bath time, start with <a href=\"/grooming-an-anxious-dog/\">if your dog hates the bath</a>.</p>", "typography_typography": "custom", "__globals__": {"typography_typography": "globals/typography?id=secondary"}}, "elements": []}, {"id": "55fbf79", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "image", "settings": {"image": {"id": 27, "url": "https://grooming-dogs.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/pexels-photo-20741414.jpeg", "alt": "A French Bulldog standing in a kitchen sink while its owner steadies it, with its head kept dry.", "source": "library"}, "image_size": "large", "caption_source": "custom", "caption": "Photo: David Kanigan / Pexels", "caption_color": "#5B6870", "caption_typography_typography": "custom", "__globals__": {"caption_color": "globals/colors?id=secondary", "caption_typography_typography": "globals/typography?id=accent"}}, "elements": []}, {"id": "b95fcb2", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 8, "column": "8", "row": "8", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "24", "right": "24", "bottom": "24", "left": "24", "isLinked": true}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "16", "right": "16", "bottom": "16", "left": "16", "isLinked": true}, "border_radius": {"unit": "px", "top": "8", "right": "8", "bottom": "8", "left": "8", "isLinked": true}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#F5F7F8", "border_border": "solid", "border_width": {"unit": "px", "top": "1", "right": "1", "bottom": "1", "left": "1", "isLinked": true}, "border_color": "#D9E0E4", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurfs", "border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdborder"}}, "elements": [{"id": "07a35e4", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>Short answer:</strong></p>\n<ol><li>Brush your dog first, because water makes mats worse.</li><li>Wet the coat with warm water.</li><li>Work in a shampoo made for dogs from the neck backward, keeping it out of the eyes and ears.</li><li>Rinse until no shampoo is left.</li><li>Towel-dry, then use a dryer on a cool or low setting if you need one, held away from the skin.</li><li>Wash the face separately with a damp cloth.</li></ol>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "66cc8d4", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "fb8d7a3", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Before the bath", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "before-the-bath"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "91d00e5", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>Brush first.</strong> Water makes mats worse <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a></sup>. Wet mats tighten as they dry and pull on the skin <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>. Brush the coat out completely before your dog gets wet. If you find tight mats, don't bathe over them. See <a href=\"/brushing-your-dog/\">brush out the coat first</a> or ask a groomer.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "25ecdb4", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>Set up the space.</strong> Choose a warm room, and get everything ready before you bring your dog in, so you never have to leave them alone in the tub. A non-slip mat in the bath or shower helps your dog feel steady. Don't bathe your dog outdoors when the weather is cool or cold: it can cause a dangerous drop in body temperature <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "afcdca0", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 8, "column": "8", "row": "8", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "24", "right": "24", "bottom": "24", "left": "24", "isLinked": true}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "16", "right": "16", "bottom": "16", "left": "16", "isLinked": true}, "border_radius": {"unit": "px", "top": "8", "right": "8", "bottom": "8", "left": "8", "isLinked": true}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#F5F7F8", "border_border": "solid", "border_width": {"unit": "px", "top": "1", "right": "1", "bottom": "1", "left": "1", "isLinked": true}, "border_color": "#D9E0E4", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurfs", "border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdborder"}}, "elements": [{"id": "51c1b85", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>What you'll need</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Shampoo made for dogs</li><li>Towels (a microfiber towel absorbs well)</li><li>A non-slip mat for the tub or shower</li><li>A cup, jug or handheld shower to wet and rinse</li><li>A soft cloth or cotton balls for the face</li><li>A hair dryer with a cool or low setting (optional)</li><li>Treats</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}, {"id": "4f71970", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Choosing a dryer or other equipment? See <a href=\"/dog-grooming-tools/\">choosing a dryer and bathing kit</a>.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "a6a21e7", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "50e941f", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Bathing your dog, step by step", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "bathing-your-dog-step-by-step"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "a709115", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<ol><li><strong>Wet the coat thoroughly with warm water</strong> <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>. Use comfortably warm water, never hot, and wet right down to the skin. Leave the head for last, or wash it separately (see below).</li><li><strong>Apply a mild shampoo made for dogs, working from the neck backward</strong> <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>. Keep shampoo out of your dog's eyes and ears <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Massage the shampoo through the coat</strong> <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>, down to the skin, including the chest, belly, legs and tail.</li><li><strong>Rinse completely</strong> (see the next section).</li><li><strong>Towel-dry before your dog leaves the bath area,</strong> then finish drying (see \"Drying your dog\").</li></ol>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "c959172", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Calm, steady handling and a few treats help. If your dog panics or struggles, stop, and see <a href=\"/grooming-an-anxious-dog/\">grooming a dog who hates being groomed</a> before you try again.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "c2ebd8f", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "8e4789c", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Rinsing thoroughly", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "rinsing-thoroughly"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "fd98015", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Rinse until there's no shampoo left in the coat. Leftover shampoo can irritate the skin <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>. Rinsing usually takes longer than the wash itself, so keep going until the water runs clear and the coat no longer feels slippery. Pay extra attention to:</p>\n<ul><li>the armpits, belly and between the back legs;</li><li>under the tail;</li><li>around the neck and collar area.</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "4f22bab", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>If your dog is itchy or smells off after a bath, see <a href=\"/dog-grooming-problems/\">itching or smell after a bath</a>.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "04bf515", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "90494e7", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Drying your dog", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "drying-your-dog"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "37b0848", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Drying matters as much as washing. Your dog should be fully dry before going outside in cool weather or settling down for the night.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "4cd9147", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Towel drying", "header_size": "h3"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "d1fa9d3", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Start with a towel <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>. Press and squeeze the water out of the coat rather than rubbing hard, which can tangle long or curly hair. A microfiber towel absorbs well <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a></sup>.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "908b4e4", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Using a dryer safely", "header_size": "h3"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "3046b18", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>A hair dryer is optional. If you use one:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Towel-dry first,</strong> then switch to a cool setting <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup> or a low setting <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a></sup>. Hot dryers can burn a dog's skin <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Keep the dryer moving</strong> back and forth, and hold it away from your dog's skin <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Go by your dog's coat and comfort</strong> when deciding whether to use a dryer at all <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>. If the noise upsets your dog, towel-dry and keep them somewhere warm instead.</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "dca3f96", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 8, "column": "8", "row": "8", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "24", "right": "24", "bottom": "24", "left": "24", "isLinked": true}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "16", "right": "16", "bottom": "16", "left": "16", "isLinked": true}, "border_radius": {"unit": "px", "top": "8", "right": "8", "bottom": "8", "left": "8", "isLinked": true}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#FBF8F3", "border_border": "solid", "border_width": {"unit": "px", "top": "0", "right": "0", "bottom": "0", "left": "4", "isLinked": false}, "border_color": "#8A5A00", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurfw", "border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdwarn"}}, "elements": [{"id": "1f75a7a", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Never point a hot dryer at your dog's skin, and never leave a dryer running on a dog unattended.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}, {"id": "d47ecc0", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Making sure your dog dries fully", "header_size": "h3"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "a30bcf4", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Thick and long coats can take a while to dry all the way down to the skin. Keep your dog somewhere warm until they're completely dry. What your dog's coat needs is explained in <a href=\"/dog-coat-types/\">dog coat types</a>.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "83fcfd3", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "94ac6b6", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Choosing a shampoo", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "choosing-a-shampoo"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "6525291", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>Use a shampoo made for dogs.</strong> Dog care organizations consistently recommend dog-specific products <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a></sup>. Here's why human shampoo isn't a good substitute <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>:</p>\n<ul><li>Human hair products aren't designed for pets.</li><li>Your dog will lick their coat, and human shampoo isn't made with that in mind.</li><li>Some ingredients in human shampoos, such as tea tree oil or anti-dandruff ingredients, may be too harsh for a dog's skin.</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "d99e2d7", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>What about baby shampoo?</strong> If you've run out of dog shampoo and have to bathe your dog now, the Animal Medical Center advises using only a no-tears baby product <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>. Treat it as a one-off. Switch back to a dog shampoo for regular baths <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "6583c3c", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 8, "column": "8", "row": "8", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "24", "right": "24", "bottom": "24", "left": "24", "isLinked": true}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "16", "right": "16", "bottom": "16", "left": "16", "isLinked": true}, "border_radius": {"unit": "px", "top": "8", "right": "8", "bottom": "8", "left": "8", "isLinked": true}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#FBF8F3", "border_border": "solid", "border_width": {"unit": "px", "top": "0", "right": "0", "bottom": "0", "left": "4", "isLinked": false}, "border_color": "#8A5A00", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurfw", "border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdwarn"}}, "elements": [{"id": "5528a53", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>Medicated shampoos:</strong> use these only if your vet recommends them, and follow the vet's instructions.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}, {"id": "a747d51", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>One dirty patch?</strong> You don't always need a full bath. For a muddy paw or a single dirty spot, a spot cleaner, waterless shampoo or wipe made for pets may be enough <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "1b024d6", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "a05e9c0", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Washing the face and around the ears", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "washing-the-face-and-around-the-ears"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "efaaa47", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Faces need a gentler approach than the body.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "e65e436", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<ul><li><strong>Use a damp cloth or cotton ball</strong> to wipe the face and around the eyes, rather than pouring water or shampoo over the head <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Keep shampoo and water out of the eyes and ears,</strong> and never push anything into them <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a></sup>. Shampoo in the eyes can cause irritation, or a painful injury to the surface of the eye <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>For dogs with facial folds or wrinkles,</strong> such as Pugs and Shar-Peis, clean the folds gently with damp cotton and dry thoroughly between them <sup><a href=\"#s4\" aria-label=\"Source 4\">[4]</a></sup>.</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "7c6d5b3", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 8, "column": "8", "row": "8", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "24", "right": "24", "bottom": "24", "left": "24", "isLinked": true}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "16", "right": "16", "bottom": "16", "left": "16", "isLinked": true}, "border_radius": {"unit": "px", "top": "8", "right": "8", "bottom": "8", "left": "8", "isLinked": true}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#FBF8F3", "border_border": "solid", "border_width": {"unit": "px", "top": "0", "right": "0", "bottom": "0", "left": "4", "isLinked": false}, "border_color": "#8A5A00", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurfw", "border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdwarn"}}, "elements": [{"id": "77f6c0e", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<ul><li><strong>Eyes:</strong> if your dog is squinting, keeps an eye closed, or the eye looks red or sore after a bath, contact your vet.</li><li><strong>Ears:</strong> watch for redness, discharge, an unusual smell or pawing at the ears, especially in dogs with floppy ears. Contact a vet if you notice them <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a></sup>.</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}, {"id": "b65bd42", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Routine ear care is covered in <a href=\"/cleaning-dog-ears/\">cleaning your dog's ears</a>.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "4333e28", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "d1bd83a", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Common questions", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "common-questions"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "4eca1f5", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "accordion", "settings": {"tabs": [{"_id": "5d7f74e", "tab_title": "How do I bathe my dog without a bathtub?", "tab_content": "<p>A walk-in shower with a handheld showerhead and a non-slip mat works well, and small dogs can often be washed in a large sink. Outdoors, use a hose only in warm weather: bathing outdoors in cool or cold weather can dangerously lower your dog's body temperature <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>. For a single dirty spot, a pet spot cleaner or waterless shampoo may do instead of a full bath <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>.</p>"}, {"_id": "19c6808", "tab_title": "Should I bathe my dog before or after a haircut?", "tab_content": "<p>Before. Brush, bathe and dry your dog thoroughly first, then trim <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a></sup>. A clean, dry, brushed coat shows you what actually needs trimming. See <a href=\"/dog-haircuts-and-trimming/\">trimming and haircuts at home</a>.</p>"}, {"_id": "d564f74", "tab_title": "Can I use a hair dryer on my dog?", "tab_content": "<p>Yes, with care. Towel-dry first, then use a cool or low setting <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>. Keep the dryer moving and away from the skin, because a hot dryer can burn <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>. If your dog is frightened by the noise, towel-dry and keep them warm instead.</p>"}], "title_html_tag": "h3", "faq_schema": "yes", "selected_icon": {"value": "fas fa-plus", "library": "fa-solid"}, "selected_active_icon": {"value": "fas fa-minus", "library": "fa-solid"}, "border_color": "#D9E0E4", "title_color": "#17324D", "tab_active_color": "#17324D", "__globals__": {"border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdborder", "title_color": "globals/colors?id=primary", "tab_active_color": "globals/colors?id=primary"}}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "bebfb32", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#F5F7F8", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurfs"}}, "elements": [{"id": "4e95a6c", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p class=\"gd-label\" id=\"next\"><strong>Where to go next</strong></p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "0d0df9a", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "row", "flex_wrap": "wrap", "flex_direction_mobile": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}}, "elements": [{"id": "9df3d72", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 8, "column": "8", "row": "8", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "24", "right": "24", "bottom": "24", "left": "24", "isLinked": true}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "16", "right": "16", "bottom": "16", "left": "16", "isLinked": true}, "border_radius": {"unit": "px", "top": "8", "right": "8", "bottom": "8", "left": "8", "isLinked": true}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#FFFFFF", "border_border": "solid", "border_width": {"unit": "px", "top": "1", "right": "1", "bottom": "1", "left": "1", "isLinked": true}, "border_color": "#D9E0E4", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurf", "border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdborder"}, "width": {"unit": "%", "size": 48}, "width_mobile": {"unit": "%", "size": 100}}, "elements": [{"id": "36e8e1d", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong><a href=\"/brushing-your-dog/\">How to brush your dog properly</a></strong></p><p>Brush before every bath. Here's how to do it to the skin.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}, {"id": "0525346", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 8, "column": "8", "row": "8", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "24", "right": "24", "bottom": "24", "left": "24", "isLinked": true}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "16", "right": "16", "bottom": "16", "left": "16", "isLinked": true}, "border_radius": {"unit": "px", "top": "8", "right": "8", "bottom": "8", "left": "8", "isLinked": true}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#FFFFFF", "border_border": "solid", "border_width": {"unit": "px", "top": "1", "right": "1", "bottom": "1", "left": "1", "isLinked": true}, "border_color": "#D9E0E4", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurf", "border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdborder"}, "width": {"unit": "%", "size": 48}, "width_mobile": {"unit": "%", "size": 100}}, "elements": [{"id": "5568029", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong><a href=\"/how-often-should-you-groom-your-dog/\">How often to groom your dog</a></strong></p><p>How often your dog's coat needs a bath.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}, {"id": "fc9923f", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 8, "column": "8", "row": "8", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "24", "right": "24", "bottom": "24", "left": "24", "isLinked": true}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "16", "right": "16", "bottom": "16", "left": "16", "isLinked": true}, "border_radius": {"unit": "px", "top": "8", "right": "8", "bottom": "8", "left": "8", "isLinked": true}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#FFFFFF", "border_border": "solid", "border_width": {"unit": "px", "top": "1", "right": "1", "bottom": "1", "left": "1", "isLinked": true}, "border_color": "#D9E0E4", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurf", "border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdborder"}, "width": {"unit": "%", "size": 48}, "width_mobile": {"unit": "%", "size": 100}}, "elements": [{"id": "451d507", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong><a href=\"/cleaning-dog-ears/\">Cleaning your dog's ears</a></strong></p><p>Bath time is a good moment to check the ears.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}, {"id": "0bd5b76", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 8, "column": "8", "row": "8", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "24", "right": "24", "bottom": "24", "left": "24", "isLinked": true}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "16", "right": "16", "bottom": "16", "left": "16", "isLinked": true}, "border_radius": {"unit": "px", "top": "8", "right": "8", "bottom": "8", "left": "8", "isLinked": true}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#FFFFFF", "border_border": "solid", "border_width": {"unit": "px", "top": "1", "right": "1", "bottom": "1", "left": "1", "isLinked": true}, "border_color": "#D9E0E4", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurf", "border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdborder"}, "width": {"unit": "%", "size": 48}, "width_mobile": {"unit": "%", "size": 100}}, "elements": [{"id": "0cc74ac", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong><a href=\"/dog-grooming-problems/\">Problems after grooming</a></strong></p><p>Itchy or smelly after a bath? Start here.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}], "isInner": true}, {"id": "4aa33a5", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>This is general information about grooming healthy dogs, not veterinary advice. If your dog has a skin, eye or ear problem, or is in pain, contact your vet. <a href=\"/editorial-policy/\">How we write, source and fund our guides</a>.</p>", "text_color": "#5B6870", "__globals__": {"typography_typography": "globals/typography?id=accent", "text_color": "globals/colors?id=secondary"}}, "elements": []}, {"id": "dc090c4", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p class=\"gd-label\" id=\"sources\"><strong>Sources</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"gd-sources\"><li id=\"s1\"><span class=\"gd-src-label\">[1]</span> AKC Staff, American Kennel Club: \"How to Groom Your Dog at Home: Easy Tips for Everyday Care\", published January 17, 2023, updated September 2, 2026. <a href=\"https://www.akc.org/expert-advice/health/how-to-groom-a-dog/\">https://www.akc.org/expert-advice/health/how-to-groom-a-dog/</a></li><li id=\"s2\"><span class=\"gd-src-label\">[2]</span> Humane World for Animals: \"How to groom your dog at home\" (undated). <a href=\"https://www.humaneworld.org/en/resources/how-groom-your-dog-home\">https://www.humaneworld.org/en/resources/how-groom-your-dog-home</a></li><li id=\"s3\"><span class=\"gd-src-label\">[3]</span> Ann Hohenhaus, DVM, The Animal Medical Center (New York): \"Can Bath Time be Dangerous for Pets?\", November 30, 2016. <a href=\"https://www.amcny.org/blog/2016/11/30/can-bath-time-dangerous-pets/\">https://www.amcny.org/blog/2016/11/30/can-bath-time-dangerous-pets/</a></li><li id=\"s4\"><span class=\"gd-src-label\">[4]</span> ASPCA: \"At-Home Pet Grooming: Top Tips and Recommendations\", April 9, 2020. <a href=\"https://www.aspca.org/news/home-pet-grooming-top-tips-and-recommendations\">https://www.aspca.org/news/home-pet-grooming-top-tips-and-recommendations</a></li></ul>", "text_color": "#5B6870", "__globals__": {"typography_typography": "globals/typography?id=accent", "text_color": "globals/colors?id=secondary"}}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}]